<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruwanwelisaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Mahathupa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ruwanwelisaya is a great stupa at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anuradhapura">Anuradhapura</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, begun by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutugemunu">Dutugemunu</a> in the 2nd century BCE and completed under his brother Saddhatissa. Built to enshrine relics of the Buddha, it is one of the most venerated monuments of Sri Lankan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>. Its white dome was restored in the 20th century.</p></div>
